{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/DSimp/App.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.DSimp.dsimpAppArgs\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">DSimp</span>.<span class=\"name\">dsimpAppArgs</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/DSimp/DSimpM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.DSimp.DSimpM\">DSimpM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/DSimp/DSimpM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.DSimp.Result\">Result</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Walks the application spine and `dsimp`s each argument unless `ProofInstInfo` marks it\nas a proof or instance. The function head itself is not recursively simplified, so\n`pre`/`post` simprocs that rewrite heads (e.g. `zetaDelta` for let-bound `.fvar` heads,\nor beta for lambda heads) must match on the whole application.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/DSimp/App.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.DSimp.dsimpAppArgs","kind":"def","line":36,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.DSimp.dsimpAppArgs","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/DSimp/App.lean#L36-L69"}}],"imports":["Init.Omega","Lean.Meta.Sym.AlphaShareBuilder","Lean.Meta.Sym.DSimp.DSimpM","Lean.Meta.Sym.DSimp.Result","Lean.Meta.Sym.ProofInstInfo"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.DSimp.App"}